						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13878275/the-midas-brick">The Midas Brick</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828418">
									

<p>Hey there DrGreywhind, I'll be critting your idea today!<br />
Note that I am neither a particularly experienced nor an offical reviewer, so take everything I say with a grain of salt. With that being said, let's begin the crit!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">*sparkly&nbsp;noises*</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'd like to start off by assuring you that SCPs don't have to be an immediate threat to humanity, the world, or reality itself (in fact, almost all of them aren't). A non-dangerous Safe-class SCP has just as much potential to be interesting, if not moreso, than some super-deadly Keter.</p>
<p>Next, I'd like to address your idea. I agree with Zaihan that the idea is underwhelming, but for different reasons. Firstly, it's not very original (as you said, it shares many similarities with <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-409">SCP-409</a>, and also <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1015">SCP-1015</a>). In fact, it is almost a clone of both mentioned SCPs in that it transmutes the people (or objects) it touches into the material it consists of.</p>
<p>Secondly, the backstory implies the existence of Kind Midas at some point (despite his status as a mythological figure) and also that the brick's existence was covered up somehow (despite it turning everything to gold). These are both pretty hefty logical issues which I'd like for you to fix.</p>
<p>I'd recommend 2 things:<br />
1. Checking out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/comprehensive-guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for some great essays on stuff like ideation and story-ing!<br />
2. Contacting some reviewers from the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a>. They've got tonnes of experience and are quite helpful!</p>
<p>And finally, to sum up your idea in one sentence<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-739506-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-739506-1')">1</a></sup>:<br />
A golden block of wood (the first thing Midas touched) gained his abilities.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
Anyway, that's it for my crit today. Thanks for reading, and I hope this helps!
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-739506-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-739506-1')">1</a>. This is to help you get an idea of the bare bones of what a critter sees when they read your summary. You may find something here that you don't like, or realise we're getting the wrong impression.</div>
</div>

							</div>

								
					
