					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harryblank" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6479803); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6479803&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606397539" alt="HarryBlank" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6479803)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harryblank" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6479803); return false;" >HarryBlank</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606382481 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Nov 2020 09:21</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-5494/comments/show">SCP-5494</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828412">
									

<p>Thanks for the read, the vote and most importantly by far, the comment.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Thoughts!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Begone,&nbsp;thoughts!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I agree that this piece takes a hit from the fact that it's being written by someone who can't provide an indigenous perspective, won't try to puppeteer one, and won't change his approach to suit what he <em>can</em> provide. That was pretty much intentional; the only way I knew how to tell the story about cultural appropriation I wanted to tell was to tread the line, just as you describe, and hope that the message that came through worked well enough for most people to make it worthwhile.</p>
<p>Ideally, someone who actually is from the related cultures would see this, and be interested in providing the missing perspective themselves in their writing. I would love to see people who have actual experience with the subject matter writing about it, whether in completely original form or making use of this piece as a springboard if necessary. Barring that, this will stand as my imperfect but hopefully not valueless intervention on the issues. I wouldn't have done it at all, except that I imagined someone taking this mythological creature and writing a bog-standard horror tale using it. This was my attempt to head that off at the pass.</p>
<p>I don't intend to write anything further on a wholly indigenous topic, and was very leery about writing this one; I had some angry points I wanted to make, though, so I made them and hoped that my intent would shine through. It seems to have.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I very much appreciate your taking the time to dissect what I wrote, and am 100% on the same page with you about the results (although I probably like it more than you do :P) The next SCP I wrote, <a href="/scp-5520">SCP-5520</a>, was an oblique take on something I had personal experience with&#8230; though, it turns out, not as personal as one of my readers.</p>

							</div>

								
					
